engine integration:
  claude:
    wrote .claude/settings.json: added extraKnownMarketplaces."gabo-ai", enabledPlugins."gabo@gabo-ai"
  codex:
    wrote .codex/config.toml: added marketplaces.gabo-ai.source_type, marketplaces.gabo-ai.source, plugins."gabo@gabo-ai".enabled
  opencode:
    no .opencode/plugins/gabo-stage-gate.js yet; nothing written
  pi:
    wrote .pi/settings.json: added packages entry npm:@gabo-ai/pi@0.2.6
    gabo refuses to build on Pi without a subagent package:
    Pi has no subagents, so gabo cannot work on Pi without a subagent package. For subagents I recommend gentle-pi, installed with `npm i -g gentle-pi` (adds the `gentle-shell` launcher) or `pi install npm:gentle-pi` (inside plain Pi); another subagent package is acceptable. As the recommended setup I recommend the full Gentle AI framework (https://github.com/Gentleman-Programming/gentle-ai): its methodology with RDD and the Engram memory stack, set up for Pi with `gentle-ai install --agent pi`. Then ask me to rebuild.
you still need to:
  - claude: trust this project folder in Claude Code so the gabo-ai marketplace and the gabo plugin apply
  - codex: trust the project in Codex so it loads .codex/config.toml
  - codex: trust both gabo hooks in /hooks
  - codex: if Codex does not list the gabo plugin after trust, run: codex plugin marketplace add testeos-z/gabo-ai
  - codex: if Codex does not list the gabo plugin after trust, run: codex plugin add gabo@gabo-ai
  - opencode: ask your agent to build the agents with gabo-runtime-opencode (it installs .opencode/plugins/gabo-stage-gate.js and the project-level experimental.subagent_depth key)
  - pi: trust the project in Pi so it installs and loads @gabo-ai/pi from .pi/settings.json
  - pi: install a subagent package (see the refusal above)
